# Help desk impersonation to AD CS ESC1 / ESC8 abuse (Microsoft Security Research, 2026-10-30) - generic heuristics (Suricata 7.x)
# Author: Jarmi
# Date: 2026-11-13
# Reference: https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/10/30/help-desk-impersonation-ad-cs-abuse-investigating-esc1-esc8-intrusion-paths/
#
# Honesty: Microsoft published NO network indicators for this activity (no IPs, domains, SFTP host, URLs
# or user agents). Every rule below is a generic, low-confidence behavioural heuristic built from the
# narrative plus standard protocol knowledge, and none has been tested against traffic. The initial
# access (Teams + Quick Assist) runs over Microsoft cloud services and is not usefully visible here.
#   - 9993001: file server opening SSH/SFTP (tcp/22) to the internet (Rclone SFTP exfiltration path).
#   - 9993002: DCE/RPC bind to the MS-EFSR interface (c681d488-d850-11d0-8c52-00c04fd90f7e) on a domain
#              controller from a non-DC host (PetitPotam-style coercion). Only sensors that see east-west
#              SMB/RPC to DCs will fire; encrypted SMB3 sessions hide the bind. Legitimate remote EFS use
#              exists but is rare against DCs.
#   - 9993004: same MS-EFSR bind carried over SMB named pipes (PetitPotam normally uses \\pipe\\efsrpc or
#              \\pipe\\lsarpc over SMB); 9993002 covers DCERPC over plain TCP. Keep both.
#   - 9993003: HTTP request to AD CS Web Enrollment (/certsrv/) from a host outside the approved
#              enrollment client list. In the ESC8 case the relayed request reaches /certsrv from the
#              attacker machine. If you enabled HTTPS + EPA (recommended mitigation) this cleartext rule
#              only sees residual HTTP and doubles as a "web enrollment still on HTTP" check.
#
# Custom variables (define in suricata.yaml address-groups):
#   $FILE_SERVERS      - file servers holding shares (exfiltration source in the ESC1 case)
#   $DC_SERVERS        - domain controllers
#   $ADCS_WEB_SERVERS  - servers hosting AD CS Web Enrollment (/certsrv)
#   $ENROLL_CLIENTS    - hosts allowed to use web enrollment (admins / jump hosts); never include DCs

alert tcp $FILE_SERVERS any -> $EXTERNAL_NET 22 (msg:"Generic heuristic - file server opening SSH/SFTP session to external host (possible Rclone SFTP exfiltration, help desk impersonation to AD CS intrusion)"; flow:established,to_server; content:"SSH-"; depth:4; reference:url,www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/10/30/help-desk-impersonation-ad-cs-abuse-investigating-esc1-esc8-intrusion-paths/; classtype:policy-violation; sid:9993001; rev:1; metadata:author Jarmi, created_at 2026_11_13, confidence low;)

alert dcerpc !$DC_SERVERS any -> $DC_SERVERS any (msg:"Generic heuristic - DCE/RPC bind to MS-EFSR (EFSRPC) interface on a domain controller (possible PetitPotam-style authentication coercion, ESC8 path)"; flow:established,to_server; dcerpc.iface:c681d488-d850-11d0-8c52-00c04fd90f7e; reference:url,www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/10/30/help-desk-impersonation-ad-cs-abuse-investigating-esc1-esc8-intrusion-paths/; classtype:attempted-admin; sid:9993002; rev:1; metadata:author Jarmi, created_at 2026_11_13, confidence low;)

alert http !$ENROLL_CLIENTS any -> $ADCS_WEB_SERVERS any (msg:"Generic heuristic - HTTP request to AD CS Web Enrollment /certsrv/ from host outside approved enrollment clients (possible NTLM relay to web enrollment, ESC8)"; flow:established,to_server; http.uri; content:"/certsrv/"; nocase; startswith; reference:url,www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/10/30/help-desk-impersonation-ad-cs-abuse-investigating-esc1-esc8-intrusion-paths/; classtype:attempted-admin; sid:9993003; rev:1; metadata:author Jarmi, created_at 2026_11_13, confidence low;)

alert smb !$DC_SERVERS any -> $DC_SERVERS any (msg:"Generic heuristic - MS-EFSR (EFSRPC) interface bind over SMB named pipe on a domain controller (possible PetitPotam-style authentication coercion, ESC8 path)"; flow:established,to_server; dcerpc.iface:c681d488-d850-11d0-8c52-00c04fd90f7e; reference:url,www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/10/30/help-desk-impersonation-ad-cs-abuse-investigating-esc1-esc8-intrusion-paths/; classtype:attempted-admin; sid:9993004; rev:1; metadata:author Jarmi, created_at 2026_11_13, confidence low;)
